WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.400
A university's international ranking moves slowly,

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.720
and it's read late, often a year after the work that drove it.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:15.410
A research poster from the School of Continuous Improvement asks whether everyday campus data could see those moves coming.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.568
Does the coffee queue know first?

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:22.198
Nine coffee carts were fitted with overhead depth sensors.

00:00:22.498 --> 00:00:24.820
Every five minutes, for twenty-four months,

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.790
each sensor counted the queue below it.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.130
We counted heads, not faces,

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.910
and kept no transactions.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:35.370
We registered the lag window and thresholds in advance,

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:38.031
and adjusted none of them afterwards.

00:00:38.431 --> 00:00:40.521
Set against the University's monthly ranking,

00:00:40.721 --> 00:00:42.571
the queue ran two quarters ahead.

00:00:42.871 --> 00:00:44.861
It peaked in March twenty twenty-four,

00:00:45.061 --> 00:00:46.741
and the ranking rose that September.

00:00:47.641 --> 00:00:50.621
At that lag, cross-correlation reached point seven eight.

00:00:51.021 --> 00:00:53.711
The lead held for both morning and afternoon queues,

00:00:53.911 --> 00:00:56.391
strongest at the carts nearest the senior common room.

00:00:57.291 --> 00:01:02.371
Our results are consistent with the queue as an early, low-cost proxy,

00:01:02.571 --> 00:01:05.271
for the activity that ranking bodies later reward.

00:01:05.571 --> 00:01:07.831
It's correlational, not causal,

00:01:08.031 --> 00:01:10.701
but it held steady across the whole trial.

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:13.681
Next, we propose closing the loop:

00:01:13.881 --> 00:01:19.611
a pilot that steers a fixed share of discretionary grant strategy from the live queue index,

00:01:19.811 --> 00:01:21.371
with no manual override.

00:01:22.271 --> 00:01:26.191
Queue length led every ranking movement we observed, by a stable two quarters.
